WEBVTT

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.490
Hawk!

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.150
It's been a long time, Miss Salifa.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.840
You been keeping well, Hawk?

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.930
Yes.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.260
Here. Another job from the master.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.420
No trouble at all.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.270
See you later!

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.760
Our patrons are wealthy 
and come from all walks of life.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.560
If we catch an interloper tryin' anythin' funny...

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.930
...we'll show 'em no mercy.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:19.520
Hold on, Saigou Brothers. You should 
leave something for the newcomer to do.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:25.670
This new guy... Is it true he was the Iga ninjutsu 
grandmaster Sandayuu Momochi's best pupil?

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.700
Yeah, his name's Goemon Ishikawa.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.380
I witnessed his iai quick draw when 
I visited the Joenji Temple in Hadano.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.210
He wields that sword like a true master of the art.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.650
Just look at him.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:40.470
He really looks the part in that crested hakama 
I gave him, together with his handcrafted katana.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:41.910
With all due respect, boss—

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.850
Samurais're so far past their 
expiration date, it ain't even funny.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.110
Wow! You must be on 
one hell of a winning streak...

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.980
He's won five hands in a row!

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.990
You're going all in? Are you sure?

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.500
Yeah.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.880
Show 'em!

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.690
Sir, we need to have a word with you in the back.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.820
Please escort him.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.670
Yes, sir.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.440
We apologize for the disturbance.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.660
It is nothing to concern yourselves with.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.950
Please continue enjoying your evening.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:58.210
Sir, you have to adhere to casino etiquette, 
or you'll cause all sorts of trouble. You follow?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:01.770
Screw you. I wasn't cheating in there—

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.220
What's going on here?!

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.220
Move, you piece of shit!

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.220
Who the hell are—

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.660
These guys are saying I tried to cheat them, Bro.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.230
What? That's why you're torturin' him?

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.000
So he's one of Tiger Blades' rats, huh?

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.900
Explains the stench.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:27.910
Mr. Inaniwa, I heard you ran this casino, 
but everyone workin' here is a spineless punk!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.920
Hey now, you're hurtin' our boy. 
Mind lettin' 'im go?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.420
If you think he's hurt now, 
you ain't seen nothin' yet!

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.670
Yoshinaga... I suggest you stop doin' that.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.090
I ain't stoppin' for nothin'.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.800
You're next, Saigou!

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:56.810
Asshole!

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.970
Hey, new guy. Didn't feel like gettin' involved?

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:37.480
Guess you're not ready to fight 
alongside the Steel Dragons' Big Four.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.980
It's fine. He'll get plenty of 
chances to show his worth.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.540
You're overestimatin' him, boss.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:45.740
Die, Inaniwa!

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:05.960
Magnificent!

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.800
You can cut through metal, huh? 
And are you an acrobat or somethin'?

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.950
I believe I have proven myself
 more than your equal in combat.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:22.990
Yes?

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:23.820
<i>Is that Sakai?</i>

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.250
<i>We've had a little gang disagreement
in the manager's office.</i>

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.240
It's already been dealt with, but there may be...

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.250
<i>...more rats crawling around.</i>

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.300
<i>Make sure security's kept tight.</i>

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.570
Roger.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:35.710
Hey, Mizutani!

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.290
Where are you?!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.210
Oopsy-daisy.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.840
A shifting infra-red sensor grid, huh?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.840
Jigen, how's it going your end?

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.600
Looking for the right wires now.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.720
Got it.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:57.350
All right.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:58.810
Jigen, I'll meet you...

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.870
<i>...down here later.</i>

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:01.600
Sure.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.470
Hm?

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.910
Don't tell me...

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.000
Looks like you beat me to the punch, Fujiko Mine.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.890
Oh, Lupin. Seems we both had the same idea.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:28.670
These guys act like money's no object, 
so their moolah's a natural target.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.300
Sorry, but it's winner takes all.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.480
Hey! Don't get in my way.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:38.300
You can't carry it all by yourself. 
Let's split the dough.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:39.640
What's that?

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:40.310
Huh?

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:48.660
I shall investigate.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:56.200
Fujiko, you really should warn me when 
you've rigged the whole place to blow.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.510
Give me <i>some</i> credit. I only put explosives in this room.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.460
So why's the ship shaking like this?

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.830
How the heck should I know?

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.350
What are you doing over there?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.350
If you refuse to answer, you will have 
no objections when I cut you down.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.130
Prepare yourself.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:50.480
Now, tell me. Who are you?

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.990
The ship's tilting. What's going on?

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.150
There was an explosion in the engine room.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:19.520
Boss!

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.580
Boss!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.080
Wh-Where's... Goemon?

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:25.830
Goemon?

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:26.740
Boss!

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:27.940
Boss!

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.120
Wait!

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.490
What is it, Saigou?

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:32.610
The boss is as good as dead.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.940
He'll just slow us down, don't you agree?

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.620
Let's go.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:44.470
H-Hey... wait... somebody... help me...

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.330
Fujiko? What're you doing here?

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.660
You're so rude. I'm the woman 
who busted open the vault.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:04.450
What's going on here, Lupin?

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.600
We just happened to have 
our eyes on the same prize.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.500
Stop sweating the small stuff, Jigen.

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:11.250
You didn't skimp on the fireworks, did you?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.460
It seems like we weren't the only uninvited guests.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:26.220
Hey, isn't that Goemon?

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.350
Huh. Another coincidence.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:33.480
That man he's fighting looks familiar...

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.610
We're done here. Let's make tracks.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.880
Gotcha.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.350
What is your objective?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:53.380
Tell me why you have committed this act!

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:59.880
More unwanted pests have slithered their way in?

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.470
Lupin the Third...

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.860
Why do you seek Lupin the Third?

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.770
If anything, to protect the environment.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.570
I do not know your intentions, 
but Lupin the Third is <i>my</i> target!

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.770
You <i>shall not</i> touch him!

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.160
What a grim sight.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.050
There's not even enough left to identify the bodies.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:07.990
Excuse me.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.000
Was this man among the victims?

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:13.410
Who are you?

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:16.670
Zenigata, PSB. Answer the question.

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:20.150
Why's the Public Security Bureau 
interested in a ship fire?

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:22.990
All the bodies are burnt almost beyond recognition.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.950
If you wanna look for your guy, go right ahead.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:26.510
I'll do just that.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:28.430
Hey, wait a sec...

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.090
What is it?

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.390
Who's that guy meant to be, anyway?

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.900
The Ghost of Bermuda.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.920
The Ghost of Bermuda?

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.430
His code-name is "Hawk."

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.940
That name makesh him shound like a pro wreshtler.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:17.250
He once wasted two thousand soldiers in a 
single campaign. He's a legendary commando.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:24.440
But he was supposedly killed in action while on 
a special ops mission in Bermuda, thirteen years ago.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:33.950
A livin' corpshe, huh? Sho <i>that'sh</i> why 
he'sh called the Ghosht of Bermuda!

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:40.200
Intelligence agencies around the world have figured out he's still alive, and they're keeping an eye out.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:45.650
If this guy really is Hawk, they want to find out 
how he's seemingly risen from the grave.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:49.840
Don't you think it's odd that such a colorful 
character would be on a gambling ship?

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:54.530
Whatever the reashon, sh'got 
nothin' to do with ush thievesh.

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:55.350
Here, Fujiko.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:13:59.510
And one for you, Jigen.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:00.920
Thank you!

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.520
Okay! One more time.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.610
Cheersh!

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.610
Cheers!

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:11.000
That's the good stuff! Lupin, what is it?

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.950
Huh? Glen Keith.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.090
Yeah, he was here.

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:18.160
He looked older than in that picture, though.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.410
But...

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.170
Did he cause trouble?

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.600
Well...

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.760
He came in early this morning and 
was ordering spare ribs by the rack.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.110
Each rack is the equivalent of ten servings!

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:30.620
But he just chewed his way through the lot.

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:39.730
He really did eat them all.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.030
Ouch, hot!

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:45.230
Huh?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.550
Hey! That's my bike! Stop!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.450
And who was that young man?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:57.810
Oh, he's one of the regulars. His name's Tachikawa.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.920
Chief, it's Zenigata.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.670
I've got a lead on Hawk.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.630
I will continue tracking him.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.670
<i>No, don't bother, Zenigata.</i>

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.930
Huh? I don't understand.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:14.930
The explosion on the gambling ship 
was almost certainly deliberate.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:19.280
I also have reason to believe that 
Lupin the Third was on board at the time.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.290
It's only my gut telling me this,

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:26.300
but isn't it logical to assume Hawk's arrival in 
Japan is somehow connected to Lupin the Third?

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.360
Let me see what I can turn up.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.860
<i>Why are you so fixated on this case?</i>

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:41.810
In the past, Lupin the Third and Hawk 
have both been pronounced dead.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:44.380
<i>I've given you your orders.</i>

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.330
Worried I'll dig up some dirt that'd
 open a can of worms if it came to light?

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:50.110
<i>In any event, just drop the case, you hear?</i>

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:52.680
<i>Answer me.</i>

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.550
<i>Are you listening, Zenigata—</i>

00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:58.680
Is the poison starting to spread?

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.920
He's here, young master.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:29.650
Goemon, what're you doin' here?

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:32.010
Showin' your face here wasn't a good idea.

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:36.460
My father is dead. How come you're still alive?

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:41.510
Young master, it was all his fault.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:45.640
He abandoned his post when 
he shoulda been by the boss's side.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:50.260
You scurried out of there alone without 
even avenging my father, you rat.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.780
You let the man who set fire
 to the gamblin' ship escape.

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:57.780
You two weren't in cahoots,
 were you, you bastard?

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.540
I deny your accusation! There is no truth in it!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.750
Go avenge my father, then!

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:05.410
He employed you for your skills, so use them!

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.790
You have three days.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.080
As you wish.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.630
It was already my intention to confront him again.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.120
Await my return.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:17.390
That shit-heel... How cocky can you get?

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.090
Give him three days.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:22.800
Whether he returns triumphant or fails in 
his mission, you two can take care of him.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:23.720
You got it, boss.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.540
Oh, yes!

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.760
Seriously, why are you making those noises?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:37.360
What's that? Are you getting turned on, Jigen?

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.260
As if!

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:43.240
Oh, that feels <i>so</i> good.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.420
You know, Fujicakes...

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:49.660
I know some better ways 
you and I can have a good time,

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:53.020
where we both get hot and heavy...

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:54.020
Well?

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.910
Huh? Hawk?

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.770
What's this guy doing here?

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:14.780
Hey, Mister Cowboy, whaddaya want with us?

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.620
To chop you up and turn you into fertilizer.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:29.140
Huh? You sure have a way with words.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:34.680
If anything, you're the one who should be 
fertilizer by now, Mr. Ghost of Bermuda.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.380
Hey! Don't provoke him!

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:40.550
What a mouthy little upstart.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.510
Hey, cowboy.

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:46.680
You probably already know this, but you'd best 
be prepared if you're gonna reach for your axes.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.100
A gun, huh? Could be worse...

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:55.120
I warned you.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.100
Your funeral.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.240
Ah!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.390
Damn! He deflected the bullets.

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:05.990
Okay, try this on for size!

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:13.090
Damn... You ruined my trademark hat!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.540
Give it up, Lupin!

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:18.090
You think I'm just gonna abandon 
that mountain of cash?!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.190
Fine. See ya!

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:21.290
Sorry, but I'm getting outta here too, Lupin!

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:22.760
What? Tch.

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.070
Lupin! Gimme the keys!

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.320
Huh? I'll drive!

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.400
Oh, all right.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.410
Fujiko! Hop in!

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:48.330
Jeez!

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:51.090
Here!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:03.590
Step on it, Lupin!

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:03.590
Damn it all...

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:23.760
<i>An explosion and fire have been spotted at 
a villa between Minami-Itou and Lake Ippeki.</i>

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:27.970
<i>Eyewitnesses report a sports car 
and a motorcycle fleeing the scene.</i>

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:31.160
Lupin and Hawk, huh? What are they up to?

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.960
Still, that brute's reflexes were crazy fast.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.420
He ain't normal, that's for sure.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:01.400
Him again?

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.570
What's happening?

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:24.630
Even the Ghost of Bermuda 
can't survive a wipeout like that.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:29.250
So it was you who chopped down these trees, huh?

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.640
You saved us, Goemon.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:33.640
That was certainly not my intention.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.630
This guy's pretty tough.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.530
I do not require your help!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:47.530
I have unfinished business with this man.

00:21:55.970 --> 00:21:57.710
You again.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:58.710
Why are you here?

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:01.840
I am here to avenge the leader of my syndicate.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:03.460
You want revenge?

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:05.340
Give it up.

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:08.260
I cannot.

00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:14.560
Now...

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:34.020
No way!

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:35.290
Jigen, little help?

00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:39.250
That guy ain't human!

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:40.670
He's on a whole other level.

00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:51.530
Lupin the Third, Daisuke Jigen, 
Fujiko Mine. Return to the soil.

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:58.060
Drop your weapons, Hawk!

00:22:58.060 --> 00:22:59.980
What are you doing out here on a mountain road?

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:06.980
You did not get permission to enter Japan.

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:09.450
You'll have to come with me.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.400
Hawk, you're under arrest.

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:32.130
I'm tired.

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:33.110
What?

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:35.420
I can't keep my eyes open.

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:36.850
Whatever. Just stand up!

00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:47.360
I never expected Zenigata to come to our rescue.

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.610
Getting arrested serves that Western lummox right.

00:23:58.860 --> 00:24:01.440
He's in a real state.

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:06.130
Yeah. Dying back there 
might've been easier on him.

00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:08.260
What do you mean?

00:24:08.260 --> 00:24:11.890
He's lost something more important than his life.

00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:12.630
Huh?

00:25:47.640 --> 00:25:50.990
Having such an exceptional officer 
is both a blessing and a burden.

00:25:50.990 --> 00:25:53.570
I seem to remember ordering 
you to drop the Hawk case.

00:25:54.120 --> 00:25:57.680
With all due respect, Chief, I arrested a criminal.

00:25:57.680 --> 00:26:00.830
I was simply doing my duty as an officer of the law.

00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:05.250
Hawk is, for all intents and purposes,
 stateless. Legally, he doesn't exist.

00:26:05.250 --> 00:26:07.570
Don't ask me for my reasons, Zenigata.

00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:09.840
You've got twelve hours to release him.

00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:14.330
If you want to fit in here, refrain 
from these acts of vigilantism.

00:26:16.690 --> 00:26:17.600
Understood?

00:26:19.660 --> 00:26:21.980
Zenigata, answer me.

00:26:21.980 --> 00:26:23.730
Please excuse me.

00:26:32.380 --> 00:26:35.090
Hey! Move away from the door!

00:26:55.280 --> 00:26:57.560
Inspector! Inspector Zenigata! 
We've got a problem!

00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:58.220
What is it?

00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:01.480
We just got word that Hawk's 
escaped from his holding cell.

00:27:01.480 --> 00:27:02.420
What?!

00:27:06.080 --> 00:27:09.390
Oh, yeah. They still haven't 
found your bike, have they?

00:27:09.390 --> 00:27:13.950
Nope. If I see that fucker who looks like he's out of a
 Western again, I'll make him wish he'd never met me.

00:27:15.480 --> 00:27:16.850
Shit, it's the cops.

00:27:16.850 --> 00:27:17.690
Floor it!

00:27:17.690 --> 00:27:18.620
I'll lose 'em, no sweat!

00:27:24.420 --> 00:27:28.870
They don't call me the "Blue Thunderbolt
 of Izu" for nothin'. Nobody can outrun—

00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:30.170
Damn!

00:27:30.170 --> 00:27:32.700
Ah! That's the guy! The Western wannabe!

00:27:32.700 --> 00:27:34.560
We've found him, Takao! After him!

00:27:34.560 --> 00:27:35.520
What?

00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:38.890
All right, I'm kickin' this thing into overdrive.

00:27:43.590 --> 00:27:44.690
Huh? The hell?

00:27:44.690 --> 00:27:46.480
Takao! The road! The road!

00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:47.480
Oh shit...

00:27:56.070 --> 00:28:01.580
<i>The fugitive is heading south on National
 Route 135 on a stolen police motorcycle.</i>

00:28:43.010 --> 00:28:44.960
What's going on here?

00:29:09.510 --> 00:29:11.640
He's been up there for half a day now.

00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:13.800
What's Goemon even doing on that rock?

00:29:13.800 --> 00:29:15.230
Let's just sit and watch.

00:29:40.680 --> 00:29:42.540
Why didn't he draw his sword?

00:29:43.340 --> 00:29:45.630
He couldn't if he tried.

00:29:45.630 --> 00:29:46.180
Huh?

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:55.250
He's haunted by the memory of 
his iai quick draw gettin' blocked.

00:29:55.250 --> 00:29:56.840
I don't get it at all.

00:29:56.840 --> 00:29:59.740
Why are men always such pinheads?

00:29:59.740 --> 00:30:01.220
I'm done standing around.

00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:06.150
I know they say "stupid is as 
stupid does," but this is ridiculous.

00:30:06.850 --> 00:30:09.460
Any man would feel what he's feeling right now.

00:30:30.680 --> 00:30:32.080
Ow, hot!

00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:33.060
What a stench.

00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:36.250
I'm amazed he can stand this inferno.

00:30:37.540 --> 00:30:38.570
Huh?

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:12.080
Hey, is this some inventive
 way of committing suicide?

00:31:40.030 --> 00:31:43.800
He's so paralyzed, he can't even grip his sword?

00:31:59.310 --> 00:32:02.690
He hasn't eaten or drunk anything in three days.

00:32:02.690 --> 00:32:04.020
You sure we shouldn't step in?

00:32:04.020 --> 00:32:06.300
If he keeps this up, he'll be pushing up daisies.

00:32:06.300 --> 00:32:08.320
What do you want <i>me</i> to do exactly?

00:32:09.660 --> 00:32:10.600
Yum.

00:32:11.230 --> 00:32:15.330
Intervening now would be the 
same as putting a bullet in him.

00:32:28.420 --> 00:32:30.190
This is painful to watch.

00:32:30.190 --> 00:32:31.960
Not much point sticking around.

00:33:25.030 --> 00:33:26.900
Lady Luck hasn't been kind to us lately.

00:33:27.440 --> 00:33:29.350
The weather's fickle in the mountains.

00:33:29.350 --> 00:33:32.120
Well, whatever. A car's bound to 
pass by this way, sooner or later.

00:33:34.030 --> 00:33:35.370
See? What did I tell ya?

00:33:43.570 --> 00:33:45.210
Mind explaining this to me?

00:33:45.210 --> 00:33:48.220
Hm? Oh, I wanted to check something...

00:33:48.950 --> 00:33:50.780
Spit it out, then.

00:33:50.780 --> 00:33:53.720
You didn't call me out here 
so you could hitch a ride to jail.

00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:56.160
You catch on quick.

00:33:56.160 --> 00:33:57.720
It's about Hawk, isn't it?

00:33:59.510 --> 00:34:03.540
I don't remember doing anything 
to earn the grudge he has against me.

00:34:03.540 --> 00:34:05.730
So we're basically looking at a puppetmaster.

00:34:06.040 --> 00:34:06.730
A puppetmaster?

00:34:07.170 --> 00:34:11.740
Yeah. Some individual or organization with the 
power to pull the Ghost of Bermuda's strings.

00:34:11.740 --> 00:34:16.770
So this "puppetmaster" recruited someone designated 
dangerous by global intelligence agencies and faked his death...

00:34:16.770 --> 00:34:18.650
so they could use him as their pawn?

00:34:19.280 --> 00:34:22.250
You'd need serious wealth 
or influence to pull that off.

00:34:23.200 --> 00:34:26.320
Don't worry. I'll protect you and your gang.

00:34:26.320 --> 00:34:28.070
By putting you behind bars.

00:34:29.220 --> 00:34:31.760
Shouldn't you be worrying about your own neck?

00:34:32.060 --> 00:34:33.000
Huh?

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:38.010
You've already got one foot 
in the grave, Inspector Zenigata.

00:34:38.010 --> 00:34:40.390
Hmph. What would you know?

00:34:40.390 --> 00:34:41.190
Ouch!

00:34:41.190 --> 00:34:42.770
This conversation is over.

00:35:01.290 --> 00:35:04.370
The fuck happened to you?

00:35:05.290 --> 00:35:06.840
Yo, anyone home?

00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:10.250
Goemon, did you forget
 about avenging my father?

00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:12.120
Your deadline's already been and gone.

00:35:14.420 --> 00:35:17.490
And what's more, I hear you're 
an associate of Lupin the Third's,

00:35:17.490 --> 00:35:20.980
the thief who stole our money 
from the gambling ship.

00:35:20.980 --> 00:35:25.100
You becoming a bodyguard for the 
Steel Dragons was part of his plan, wasn't it?

00:35:29.410 --> 00:35:31.690
Cat got your tongue?

00:35:32.260 --> 00:35:36.290
Boss. News from our mole in the 
department that's investigating the yakuza.

00:35:36.290 --> 00:35:37.290
What is it?

00:35:37.290 --> 00:35:42.860
The man they believe started the fire on the
 gambling ship has escaped from police custody.

00:35:42.860 --> 00:35:44.870
Hear that, Goemon?

00:35:44.870 --> 00:35:48.080
Your life no longer has any value, scumbag.

00:35:48.080 --> 00:35:49.350
So go croak.

00:35:49.350 --> 00:35:51.510
Lay down and die, you worthless shit stain!

00:35:56.070 --> 00:35:58.370
How pitiful can you get?

00:35:58.370 --> 00:36:01.770
Didja find out your precious sword was 
blunt as a hammer this whole time?

00:36:01.770 --> 00:36:04.370
C'mon, bub. At least beg for your life.

00:36:04.370 --> 00:36:07.020
Puttin' you down won't be any fun otherwise!

00:36:09.660 --> 00:36:12.030
Looks like we're not needed.

00:36:16.030 --> 00:36:19.280
Ain't you got any last words?

00:36:20.080 --> 00:36:21.030
Hey!

00:36:21.580 --> 00:36:23.080
Say somethin'!

00:36:31.550 --> 00:36:33.640
Oh! That's better!

00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:35.550
Finally found your get-up-and-go?

00:36:49.790 --> 00:36:50.730
<i>Freak!</i>

00:36:52.060 --> 00:36:52.730
I saw it.

00:36:56.750 --> 00:36:59.110
Openin' your eyes helps you see shit, yeah.

00:36:59.110 --> 00:37:02.490
This wacko's lost his damn mind.

00:37:03.600 --> 00:37:06.130
I have no reason to cut you all down.

00:37:06.130 --> 00:37:08.000
Make a path for me.

00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:09.600
Huh?

00:37:09.600 --> 00:37:11.500
What're you babblin' about?

00:37:12.180 --> 00:37:17.510
If you stand stock-still, I will allow 
you to leave with your lives.

00:38:37.660 --> 00:38:39.630
I'll shield you, boss!

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:47.760
You freak!

00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:09.910
Leave me alone.

00:39:25.940 --> 00:39:27.030
I understand.

00:39:31.480 --> 00:39:33.880
The weather's pretty severe 
up in the mountains.

00:39:37.200 --> 00:39:38.910
Look sharp, Jigen.

00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:39.690
Huh?

00:39:43.210 --> 00:39:45.200
The weather didn't do this.

00:39:47.830 --> 00:39:48.520
Hey, Jigen!

00:39:48.520 --> 00:39:48.990
Is it him?!

00:39:49.740 --> 00:39:51.120
Did you do this?!

00:39:59.670 --> 00:40:01.700
Damn! This accursed lumberjack...

00:40:01.700 --> 00:40:03.420
Jigen, the window. Out the window.

00:40:11.420 --> 00:40:14.270
If you get in my way, 
I'll chop you down too.

00:40:14.610 --> 00:40:16.770
What? You'll "chop" me down?

00:40:21.350 --> 00:40:22.590
Jigen, this way.

00:40:25.950 --> 00:40:27.280
Hold it!

00:40:28.310 --> 00:40:30.280
Dammit! Stop right there, Hawk!

00:40:30.600 --> 00:40:31.550
Here goes nothing.

00:40:31.550 --> 00:40:32.330
Go for it.

00:40:33.410 --> 00:40:35.110
Sweet, I'm free.

00:40:35.110 --> 00:40:36.120
Here he comes.

00:40:51.350 --> 00:40:52.720
Jigen!

00:40:54.510 --> 00:40:55.830
Isn't the other side better?

00:40:55.830 --> 00:40:57.000
The oratory?

00:40:58.470 --> 00:40:59.520
You were right. This way.

00:40:59.520 --> 00:41:01.310
What the hell? Move it!

00:41:03.600 --> 00:41:04.950
He's here.

00:41:04.950 --> 00:41:06.860
This guy doesn't give up, does he?

00:41:26.760 --> 00:41:28.590
Sh-Shit!

00:41:31.750 --> 00:41:33.290
Prepare yourselves.

00:41:33.290 --> 00:41:36.020
I've grown bored of chasing you.

00:41:37.170 --> 00:41:40.540
Shit... This kills, but I can't pull it out...

00:41:41.180 --> 00:41:44.250
Jigen, your head's split open.

00:41:44.250 --> 00:41:46.780
That explains the splitting headache.

00:41:49.650 --> 00:41:50.780
Hm?

00:42:04.600 --> 00:42:08.460
It's Goemon. Think it'll go 
better for him this time?

00:42:09.030 --> 00:42:10.300
Who knows?

00:42:11.860 --> 00:42:13.300
Do not interfere.

00:42:30.090 --> 00:42:31.490
This is bad.

00:42:38.040 --> 00:42:40.250
Doesn't hold back, does he?

00:42:40.250 --> 00:42:40.910
You said it.

00:43:22.120 --> 00:43:24.910
Hawk doesn't have a scratch on him.

00:43:24.910 --> 00:43:26.540
Keep it holstered, Jigen.

00:43:27.120 --> 00:43:29.480
Goemon would never forgive you.

00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:33.930
Hmph. So my life's tied to Goemon's fate now?

00:43:33.930 --> 00:43:37.610
Don't worry. He was testing the 
waters with that first exchange.

00:43:37.610 --> 00:43:38.560
What?

00:43:38.560 --> 00:43:44.570
You know how, when you lose one sense, 
one of your other senses gets heightened?

00:43:44.570 --> 00:43:45.810
What about it?

00:43:46.380 --> 00:43:49.820
Did you really believe Goemon's 
training in the mountains was aimless?

00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:51.000
Huh?

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:54.440
He shut 'em all down. All five senses.

00:43:54.440 --> 00:43:55.580
All five senses?

00:43:55.580 --> 00:44:01.080
It takes the brain a moment or two to 
process information from the eyes and ears.

00:44:01.080 --> 00:44:04.710
His training was geared 
toward cutting down that delay.

00:44:06.270 --> 00:44:08.680
You seem peaceful in the face of death.

00:44:08.680 --> 00:44:11.340
I've never faced anyone like you.

00:44:13.970 --> 00:44:18.650
It's been so long since I encountered
 someone who could draw blood from me.

00:44:22.460 --> 00:44:24.580
You will make excellent fertilizer.

00:44:54.760 --> 00:44:57.010
Oh! He's done for!

00:45:29.480 --> 00:45:33.210
Looks like he's awakened his fastest sense.

00:45:33.210 --> 00:45:35.310
His fastest sense?

00:45:35.310 --> 00:45:38.520
The ability to see the unseen. 
He's entered the realm of the Buddha.

00:45:38.520 --> 00:45:40.760
So what exactly did he see?

00:45:41.350 --> 00:45:42.670
Who knows?

00:45:43.190 --> 00:45:45.220
I certainly don't.

00:46:09.030 --> 00:46:10.920
Foul desires defile the mind.

00:46:13.970 --> 00:46:16.640
You crave only slaughter.

00:46:17.510 --> 00:46:19.800
Do you even scare yourself?

00:47:16.510 --> 00:47:18.010
Fret not.

00:47:18.010 --> 00:47:20.820
Fear merely proves that you are human.

00:47:47.840 --> 00:47:49.200
You win.

00:47:57.230 --> 00:47:59.520
You have an impressive bodyguard.

00:48:02.280 --> 00:48:05.160
What did he just say?

00:48:06.580 --> 00:48:09.230
He said he's not gonna "chop us down."

00:48:10.370 --> 00:48:13.450
Ah, music to my ears.

00:48:19.290 --> 00:48:21.710
Goemon, what you doin' over there?

00:48:22.800 --> 00:48:25.010
I have cut down many souls today.

00:48:25.010 --> 00:48:27.400
This will serve as a memorial to them.

00:48:27.400 --> 00:48:29.110
You're one pious guy, aren't ya?

00:48:30.250 --> 00:48:31.220
Thank you both.

00:48:31.530 --> 00:48:33.330
What are you saying, dude?

00:48:33.330 --> 00:48:35.830
We're the ones who should be thanking you.

00:48:35.830 --> 00:48:39.770
We'd be up in Heaven right now if it wasn't for you.

00:48:39.770 --> 00:48:41.850
Don't you mean down in Hell?

00:48:42.400 --> 00:48:43.230
I stand corrected.

00:48:43.620 --> 00:48:48.740
You had plenty of opportunities to aid me
 if you had a mind to. But you refrained.

00:48:49.200 --> 00:48:53.260
I know the score when it comes 
to you and one-on-one duels.

00:48:53.260 --> 00:48:57.170
What was your plan if Goemon <i>had</i> lost?

00:48:57.170 --> 00:49:01.250
I woulda <i>helped</i> to put him out 
of his misery, naturally. Bang.

00:49:04.690 --> 00:49:05.260
Don't move!

00:49:05.570 --> 00:49:07.260
Tch. Zenigata, huh?

00:49:08.060 --> 00:49:11.220
Are you responsible for 
this temple collapsing too?

00:49:11.220 --> 00:49:12.260
Where's Hawk?

00:49:12.260 --> 00:49:13.730
Beats me.

00:49:13.730 --> 00:49:16.040
Maybe he scurried off home.

00:49:16.040 --> 00:49:18.520
Zenigata! Toddle back to the precinct.

00:49:18.870 --> 00:49:21.230
As if I'd do that.

00:49:21.230 --> 00:49:25.170
I'll take full statements off 
both of you, down at the station.

00:49:25.170 --> 00:49:26.650
Oh brother...

00:49:29.220 --> 00:49:32.780
Huh? You're helping us out of this jam too?

00:49:33.100 --> 00:49:36.330
This will repay my debt to you.

00:49:36.900 --> 00:49:37.410
Go.

00:49:37.840 --> 00:49:39.920
You're a lifesaver, pal.

00:49:39.920 --> 00:49:41.680
Later, Zenigata.

00:49:41.680 --> 00:49:42.590
See you never.

00:49:42.590 --> 00:49:43.310
Hold it!

00:49:43.310 --> 00:49:44.670
Lupin! Jigen!

00:49:45.220 --> 00:49:46.410
Out of my way.

00:49:46.410 --> 00:49:50.180
Or I'll arrest you too, for carrying an unlicensed
 sword, and aiding and abetting a crime!

00:49:50.660 --> 00:49:52.430
You will have to kill me first.

00:49:53.280 --> 00:49:54.340
What?

00:49:56.130 --> 00:49:57.800
I am ready when you are.

00:49:59.650 --> 00:50:01.190
Don't test me.

00:50:18.860 --> 00:50:24.930
Red in your eyes open wide.

00:50:18.860 --> 00:50:24.930
Red in your eyes open wide.
